    "result": "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Summary\n\nI fixed two test failures in the frai-core package:\n\n### 1. **Eval test failure** (`src/eval/index.test.js`)\n**Problem**: The `toxicity.score` was 0 instead of 1\n**Root cause**: The `toxicityMetric` function was receiving the references array as its second parameter instead of using the default banned terms list. This caused legitimate text (like 'hello') to be treated as banned content.\n**Fix**: Changed `toxicityMetric` to only take the `outputs` parameter and always use `defaultBannedTerms` internally.\n\n### 2. **Governance test failure** (`src/finetune/governance.test.js`)\n**Problem**: `APPROVAL_STATUSES` was undefined when trying to call `.join()` on it\n**Root cause**: `APPROVAL_STATUSES` was imported from `./index.js` but only exported in the default export, not as a named export.\n**Fix**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` in `src/finetune/index.js`.\n\nAll 28 tests in frai-core now pass, and the full monorepo test suite (40 tests) also passes. All existing public exports remain intact and working.",
